WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:03.200
-You look great, as always.
You're always rocking it.

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:04.934
-I'm trying to be like you, bro.
-No. Come on, buddy.

00:00:04.934 --> 00:00:07.467
Hey. Happy birthday.
Happy belated birthday.

00:00:07.467 --> 00:00:08.734
-Thank you, bro.
-Come on, buddy.

00:00:08.734 --> 00:00:11.267
If I know Maluma,
I know you probably just spent

00:00:11.267 --> 00:00:15.000
a nice quiet birthday
at home, right, just chill.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:16.334
-It was pretty relaxed.
-Yeah.

00:00:16.334 --> 00:00:17.968
I have a video of you
at your birthday.

00:00:17.968 --> 00:00:19.968
Take a look at this.
-Let me see.

00:00:19.968 --> 00:00:22.067
[ Laughter ]

00:00:22.067 --> 00:00:25.534
-Yeah, okay.
Yeah. There you go. That's --

00:00:25.534 --> 00:00:30.200
We celebrate the same way.
We celebrate the same way.

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:31.467
We're like twins.

00:00:31.467 --> 00:00:33.367
-Well, I told you it was chill,
it was relaxed.

00:00:33.367 --> 00:00:34.801
At home watching movies.

00:00:34.801 --> 00:00:36.133
-Yeah, that's all
you were doing.

00:00:36.133 --> 00:00:38.000
What was going on there?

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:40.100
-Well, was in Aspen
with my friends.

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:43.501
I went there
for like almost two weeks.

00:00:43.501 --> 00:00:47.534
And I was expecting that day
so bad. You can tell.

00:00:47.534 --> 00:00:51.267
I was pouring all champagne
on me. Yeah, man, it's nice.

00:00:51.267 --> 00:00:56.000
When you turn 28, you know,
nothing is the same.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:58.434
[ Laughter ]

00:00:58.434 --> 00:01:01.234
-You just made me so sad.
Yeah, uh...

00:01:01.234 --> 00:01:03.801
[ Laughs ] Uh...

00:01:03.801 --> 00:01:05.801
Last time,
we talked about your tour,

00:01:05.801 --> 00:01:07.868
and you talked about
you're going to go

00:01:07.868 --> 00:01:09.834
back to your hometown...
-Yes, sir.

00:01:09.834 --> 00:01:11.801
-...in Colombia and perform.

00:01:11.801 --> 00:01:13.734
-Yeah, have the biggest
concert of my career.

00:01:13.734 --> 00:01:16.067
It's going to be on April 30th,

00:01:16.067 --> 00:01:18.701
in the stadium in Medellin,
representing.

00:01:18.701 --> 00:01:20.033
Bro, I'm so happy.
For the first time.

00:01:20.033 --> 00:01:21.367
-Medellin.
-Yeah, for the first time,

00:01:21.367 --> 00:01:22.801
I'm going to perform
in my hometown.

00:01:22.801 --> 00:01:24.434
-[ Cheers and applause ]
-After ten years.

00:01:24.434 --> 00:01:26.701
-How does it feel?
How does it feel?

00:01:26.701 --> 00:01:28.367
-I'm nervous, to be honest.
-Yeah.

00:01:28.367 --> 00:01:30.601
-You know,
because it's not the same.

00:01:30.601 --> 00:01:32.701
Of course, I'm very blessed --
-You don't want to mess up.

00:01:32.701 --> 00:01:34.033
-Yeah, of course,
I'm very blessed

00:01:34.033 --> 00:01:35.634
that I've been touring
around the world,

00:01:35.634 --> 00:01:37.834
but nothing more important
than your hometown, bro.

00:01:37.834 --> 00:01:39.901
So, I'm going to get there,
and I have to kill it.

00:01:39.901 --> 00:01:41.234
-Yeah, and you're going to.

00:01:41.234 --> 00:01:42.801
-I have to. You're coming.

00:01:42.801 --> 00:01:44.367
-Of course. I'm there.
I'm opening.

00:01:44.367 --> 00:01:46.234
Yeah. I know. Yeah.
I'll get some songs ready.

00:01:46.234 --> 00:01:47.801
I'll get some songs ready.
I'll run it by you.

00:01:47.801 --> 00:01:50.767
-Okay.
-I'll bring the champagne.

00:01:50.767 --> 00:01:52.000
But you're doing it

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:53.901
in the country's
biggest soccer stadium.

00:01:53.901 --> 00:01:55.434
-Yes, sir.
-Which is bigger than --

00:01:55.434 --> 00:01:57.067
We can't even imagine it
really here.

00:01:57.067 --> 00:01:59.767
-Yeah, it's going to be like
45,000 people.

00:01:59.767 --> 00:02:00.968
-Wow.

00:02:00.968 --> 00:02:02.000
-So, yeah,
that's why I'm nervous.

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:03.300
-I was talking to you. I go,

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:04.667
"That's big. You're playing
this soccer stadium."

00:02:04.667 --> 00:02:06.534
And you go,
"Yeah, I always dreamt

00:02:06.534 --> 00:02:07.968
of being in that stadium."

00:02:07.968 --> 00:02:09.133
I go, "Oh, that's awesome."

00:02:09.133 --> 00:02:11.367
But not as Maluma,
not as a singer.

00:02:11.367 --> 00:02:13.868
-Yeah, you're right, bro.
-You played soccer.

00:02:13.868 --> 00:02:17.801
-I wanted to be a professional
soccer player when I was a kid.

00:02:17.801 --> 00:02:21.033
So I played soccer for almost,
like, eight years of my life,

00:02:21.033 --> 00:02:26.367
but when I turned 16 years old,
I decided to start making music,

00:02:26.367 --> 00:02:28.601
and now we're here, man,
you know?

00:02:28.601 --> 00:02:30.634
-Exactly.
Now you're at the stadium.

00:02:30.634 --> 00:02:32.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:34.868
-I remember I told my sister

00:02:34.868 --> 00:02:37.367
that I wanted to fill
the stadium, you know?

00:02:37.367 --> 00:02:42.100
I didn't know that I was gonna
do it performing as a musician.

00:02:42.100 --> 00:02:43.634
I said, like, at the beginning,

00:02:43.634 --> 00:02:45.400
"I'm gonna be here.
I'm gonna play soccer."

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:48.400
And then 10 years later
and coming back to my hometown,

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:51.434
going back to Medellin,
and performing for my people,

00:02:51.434 --> 00:02:53.901
my family, man, that's in--
That's crazy.

00:02:53.901 --> 00:02:55.734
-Can you still play?
-Yeah.

00:02:55.734 --> 00:02:57.601
-You can?
-You? You play soccer or not?

00:02:57.601 --> 00:03:01.334
-No. I get exhausted
watching soccer.

00:03:01.334 --> 00:03:02.734
-Really?
-It's exhausting.

00:03:02.734 --> 00:03:05.000
-I love playing soccer.
I still do it. I still do it.

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:06.701
-I mean, we have a --
I have a ball here.

00:03:06.701 --> 00:03:08.667
-No way.
-Could you --

00:03:08.667 --> 00:03:11.100
-[ Cheers and applause ]
-Okay.

00:03:11.100 --> 00:03:14.133
-Could you show me a trick
or something?

00:03:14.133 --> 00:03:16.634
-Oh, my God.
-Yeah.

00:03:16.634 --> 00:03:17.868
-I'm feeling the pressure.

00:03:17.868 --> 00:03:19.300
-Yeah, just pretend this
is the concert.

00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:20.601
-The stadium.
-This is the stadium.

00:03:20.601 --> 00:03:21.767
Everyone's -- Yeah.

00:03:21.767 --> 00:03:23.634
-[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yes!

00:03:23.634 --> 00:03:25.701
-Okay.

00:03:25.701 --> 00:03:32.100
♪♪

00:03:32.100 --> 00:03:33.901
-Come on, bud. Come on, man.

00:03:33.901 --> 00:03:37.834
Yeah, that's what I'm talk--
Yeah! Come on, bud!

00:03:37.834 --> 00:03:39.567
Let's go, man.

00:03:39.567 --> 00:03:42.601
What in the what?

00:03:42.601 --> 00:03:44.667
[ Laughter ]

00:03:44.667 --> 00:03:47.701
♪♪

00:03:47.701 --> 00:03:49.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:49.267 --> 00:03:50.767
[ Speaking indistinctly ]

00:03:50.767 --> 00:03:53.367
-Yeah, I didn't wear a cup.
I didn't wear a cup.

00:03:53.367 --> 00:03:55.200
That's Maluma right there.
Come on.

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:56.667
You know how to do it, bud.

00:03:56.667 --> 00:03:58.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:01.033 --> 00:04:04.100
-That's why I'm singing now.
-Yeah.

00:04:04.100 --> 00:04:08.267
You just became, also,
the first recording artist

00:04:08.267 --> 00:04:10.601
to design your own bottle
for Hennessy.

00:04:10.601 --> 00:04:12.167
-Yeah.
-And this is a thing --

00:04:12.167 --> 00:04:14.067
Last time you were here,

00:04:14.067 --> 00:04:15.534
you brought me a nice bottle
of Hennessy.

00:04:15.534 --> 00:04:17.634
And I go --
That was so nice of you.

00:04:17.634 --> 00:04:19.334
And it's empty now, by the way.
Thank you.

00:04:19.334 --> 00:04:21.367
We're going to debut it
right now.

00:04:21.367 --> 00:04:23.167
-Yeah, bro, yeah, please.
-No one's ever seen this.

00:04:23.167 --> 00:04:25.901
Please, please, please.
I want them to see it.

00:04:25.901 --> 00:04:28.033
I want them to see it, please.

00:04:28.033 --> 00:04:30.234
♪ Ba-da-ba-ba ♪
-♪ Da-da-da-da ♪

00:04:30.234 --> 00:04:31.968
Look at that.

00:04:31.968 --> 00:04:34.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:34.067 --> 00:04:36.300
♪♪

00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:40.067
Look at it. Look at that, bud!
-Yeah, bro.

00:04:40.067 --> 00:04:42.300
-How cool is that, man?

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:43.667
-You like it?
-I love it!

00:04:43.667 --> 00:04:46.767
Dude, for being 28 years old
and you get to do this

00:04:46.767 --> 00:04:49.167
and play stadiums, look
at what you're doing, buddy.

00:04:49.167 --> 00:04:51.100
-Well, because
I really love Hennessy...

00:04:51.100 --> 00:04:53.267
That's why I designed it.
-Yeah. Yeah. Me too.

00:04:53.267 --> 00:04:56.100
I don't get to design
my own bottle. Yeah.

00:04:56.100 --> 00:04:57.300
This looks gorgeous, bud.

00:04:57.300 --> 00:04:58.701
-Thank you, bro.
-What goes into this?

00:04:58.701 --> 00:05:00.200
I mean, do you look
at different things

00:05:00.200 --> 00:05:02.200
and you make a choice and
you go, "I don't like that"?

00:05:02.200 --> 00:05:03.934
-Yeah, remember
that I was doing

00:05:03.934 --> 00:05:06.467
the "Papi Juancho" tour
here in the States.

00:05:06.467 --> 00:05:08.934
So, I was using
a lot of these colors

00:05:08.934 --> 00:05:11.601
and also trying to put
my Latin culture

00:05:11.601 --> 00:05:13.400
and also
my Colombian culture.

00:05:13.400 --> 00:05:14.801
I'm from Medellin, Colombia,

00:05:14.801 --> 00:05:18.033
so I wanted just to
bring everything, what I am.

00:05:18.033 --> 00:05:19.934
And I feel proud
to be Latin, bro,

00:05:19.934 --> 00:05:21.934
so I put everything
in this bottle.

00:05:21.934 --> 00:05:24.434
You can -- You can see it.
I feel proud, man, you know.

00:05:24.434 --> 00:05:26.234
-Good for you, buddy.
I'm proud.

00:05:26.234 --> 00:05:28.267
-Thank you, man.
-I'm proud of you, bud.

00:05:28.267 --> 00:05:31.334
Also, I think, you know --
Not only are we besties,

00:05:31.334 --> 00:05:33.667
but also --
-What else?

00:05:33.667 --> 00:05:35.868
-We are also co-stars
in a movie.

00:05:35.868 --> 00:05:37.033
-Of course, bro.

00:05:37.033 --> 00:05:39.434
-I make a cameo
in the movie "Marry Me."

00:05:39.434 --> 00:05:41.634
-Yes, sir.
And you killed it.

00:05:41.634 --> 00:05:42.734
-Yeah.
-I remember.

00:05:42.734 --> 00:05:44.334
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
It was hard for you, no?

00:05:44.334 --> 00:05:45.467
-It was really tough.

00:05:45.467 --> 00:05:47.634
I played myself.
I played myself.

00:05:47.634 --> 00:05:50.133
I was like, "Oh, what am I going
to be like in this movie?"

00:05:50.133 --> 00:05:52.901
But look at you, though.
You do a voice in "Encanto,"

00:05:52.901 --> 00:05:54.434
the biggest movie
in the world right now.

00:05:54.434 --> 00:05:56.701
-Yeah.

00:05:56.701 --> 00:06:00.167
-Crushing right now.
-Yeah, bro.

00:06:00.167 --> 00:06:03.067
That movie is nice because
they're telling the true story

00:06:03.067 --> 00:06:04.534
about Colombia.

00:06:04.534 --> 00:06:07.601
Beautiful, beautiful things are
told in the movie "Encanto."

00:06:07.601 --> 00:06:09.567
Because I don't want people
to think

00:06:09.567 --> 00:06:12.667
that Colombia is Pablo Escobar
anymore and all violence.

00:06:12.667 --> 00:06:14.434
See "Encanto," man.
It's beautiful.

00:06:14.434 --> 00:06:15.701
-That's right.
It is beautiful.

00:06:15.701 --> 00:06:19.000
-So I feel great to be
part of the movie, too.

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:20.367
You know?
-That's awesome.

00:06:20.367 --> 00:06:21.968
Let's talk about "Marry Me."

00:06:21.968 --> 00:06:23.767
Because I'm predicting,
right now,

00:06:23.767 --> 00:06:25.334
this is going to start
a new renaissance

00:06:25.334 --> 00:06:27.901
of romantic comedies, because
it's so well done, buddy.

00:06:27.901 --> 00:06:30.067
And you and Jennifer
have chemistry.

00:06:30.067 --> 00:06:32.701
I remember we were talking
when we shot the film here.

00:06:32.701 --> 00:06:34.067
We shot a scene here.

00:06:34.067 --> 00:06:36.767
And then we went to the Garden
the night before maybe?

00:06:36.767 --> 00:06:39.167
-Yeah. The night before.
And then next day we came here.

00:06:39.167 --> 00:06:40.434
Yeah, I remember.
-Yeah.

00:06:40.434 --> 00:06:43.434
And you shot a scene
from Madison Square Garden.

00:06:43.434 --> 00:06:45.200
-Yeah, man.
-How was that?

00:06:45.200 --> 00:06:48.167
-It was nice. [ Laughs ]
-Tell the truth.

00:06:48.167 --> 00:06:50.300
-No, no, no.
-Tell the truth.

00:06:50.300 --> 00:06:51.834
-The truth -- You want me
to tell the truth?

00:06:51.834 --> 00:06:55.334
Well, I had fun,
I mean, it was nice.

00:06:55.334 --> 00:06:56.934
I was performing with Jennifer.

00:06:56.934 --> 00:07:00.400
She came like a queen,
and I just wanted to hug her,

00:07:00.400 --> 00:07:02.000
but we had a teleprompter

00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:04.033
because I didn't know
the lyrics of the song.

00:07:04.033 --> 00:07:05.467
Yeah, right.

00:07:05.467 --> 00:07:10.701
And then I started singing,
and I forgot the lyrics.

00:07:10.701 --> 00:07:15.434
And I saw the teleprompter,
and the teleprompter went off.

00:07:15.434 --> 00:07:17.400
[ Laughter ]

00:07:17.400 --> 00:07:20.067
So, it was -- it was here
at the Madison Square Garden,

00:07:20.067 --> 00:07:23.868
one of the most important
concerts of my career.

00:07:23.868 --> 00:07:26.100
But, yeah -- But Jennifer,
she held me, man.

00:07:26.100 --> 00:07:28.701
-She's a pro, right?
-Yeah, yeah, she got my back.

00:07:28.701 --> 00:07:31.667
So, at the end of the day,
like, no one realized

00:07:31.667 --> 00:07:33.434
that I didn't know the lyrics.

00:07:33.434 --> 00:07:35.501
-It's a beautiful song, though.
It's an awesome song.

00:07:35.501 --> 00:07:37.734
And you're actually coming back
here to perform it on Friday.

00:07:37.734 --> 00:07:39.200
-Yeah. Yeah, on Friday,
we're going to be here.

00:07:39.200 --> 00:07:40.267
-"Marry Me."

00:07:40.267 --> 00:07:41.701
-I'm going to move
to the studio.

00:07:41.701 --> 00:07:44.901
-Just live here. I'll give you
the keys to my apartment.

00:07:44.901 --> 00:07:46.200
You can just crash tonight.
Yeah.

00:07:46.200 --> 00:07:47.734
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:07:47.734 --> 00:07:49.868
Here's Maluma and Jennifer Lopez
in "Marry Me."

00:07:49.868 --> 00:07:51.634
Take a look at this.

00:07:51.634 --> 00:07:53.234
-♪ We could tie it up tonight ♪

00:07:53.234 --> 00:07:55.734
♪ No patience,
Take my last name ♪

00:07:55.734 --> 00:07:57.534
♪ Put it where your name is ♪

00:07:57.534 --> 00:08:00.667
♪ Have they ever seen
a love this famous? ♪

00:08:00.667 --> 00:08:03.501
-♪ They never, no, they never ♪

00:08:03.501 --> 00:08:06.400
♪ This forever, ever, ever,
ever, ever, ever ♪

00:08:06.400 --> 00:08:10.100
♪ Ain't nobody do it
better, better, better ♪

00:08:10.100 --> 00:08:12.167
♪ And it's only getting better ♪

00:08:12.167 --> 00:08:14.367
♪ True love
gotta ring, ring, ring ♪

00:08:14.367 --> 00:08:15.534
-♪ Ooh, it gotta ♪

00:08:15.534 --> 00:08:17.133
-♪ Church bells,
let 'em ring ring ring ♪

00:08:17.133 --> 00:08:20.467
-♪ Ooh, they gotta, this queen
need a king, king, king ♪

00:08:20.467 --> 00:08:22.601
-♪ For life,
for life, for life ♪

00:08:22.601 --> 00:08:25.000
-Yes! Maluma!

00:08:25.000 --> 00:08:27.501
"Marry Me" is in theaters
on February 11th,

00:08:27.501 --> 00:08:29.133
also streaming on Peacock.

